t/output pairs showing a sample invocation with expected results; risk-level and changed-services determination would benefit from a worked example. |\n| 9 | Known Gotchas | Instruction Calibration | strong | Three domain-specific pitfalls in \"Common Mistakes\" (feature-branch deploys, skipping dry-run, ignoring health warnings) each with concrete consequences and mitigations. |\n| 10 | Execution Checklist | Workflow Control | strong | Six numbered steps with halt conditions at Steps 1-3, an explicit dry-run exit point at Step 3, and a production approval gate at Step 4. |\n| 11 | Self-Correcting Loop | Workflow Control | present | Health check in Step 6 validates the deployment, but there is no retry loop, max iteration count, or automated fix-and-recheck cycle on failure. |\n| 12 | Plan-Validate-Execute | Workflow Control | strong | Clear three-phase split: planning (Steps 1-3), approval gate (Step 4 with explicit \"yes\"/\"approve\" requirement for production), and execution (Steps 5-6) with `--dry-run` preview mode. |\n| 13 | Utility Bundle | Executable Code | N/A | Skill delegates to project-provided scripts (`deploy.sh`, `health-check.sh`) rather than bundling its own; no skill-specific helper scripts needed. |\n| 14 | Autonomy Calibration | Meta | strong | `allowed-tools` restricted to Bash/Read/Write/Glob, production deployments require explicit user approval, staging auto-proceeds; risk profile matches autonomy level precisely. |\n\n**Summary**: 11 of 12 applicable patterns present, 9 of 12 strong, 3 improvements suggested\n\n### Activation Test\n\n**Description analyzed**: \"Deploy a release to staging or production environments. Use when the user asks to 'deploy', 'release', 'push to st...\"\n\n**Would trigger on**:\n- \"Deploy v1.2.3 to production\"\n- \"Push the latest build to staging\"\n- \"Promote the current build to prod\"\n\n**Should NOT trigger on**:\n- \"Roll back the last production deployment\" (routes to deploy:rollback)\n\n**Observations**: